{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CNxt5y5MFs7VbL9B9ofcQZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# mobile-android: coverage atlas (D1-D20 seen, D21+ forecast)\n2\t\n3\tScope: common Android/mobile CTF concepts mapped against what this lane has shipped and what the harness can handle.\n4\tGround truth (see `reference/techniques/mobile-android.md`): all 20 days shipped the same ~12.7 KB fixture. The day's\n5\tTHEME was flavour only (manifest `huntress.mechanic` + dex `DAY-NN:<theme>:<mechanic>`). The answer `ANS-<16 HEX>` was\n6\tin `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` behind a rotating codec (plain/reverse/base64/xor/split/hex/caesar/native/indexed/\n7\treflection) on D1-D19. D15\n8\tadded the first real extra payload (`lib/x86_64/libarena.so` with the answer as a `.rodata` literal) and mixed-day\n9\tMastery. D16 (JNI Boundary) TT/Mastery builds added the first REAL gate in code: `Java_<pkg>_JNIBoundary_nativeEvidence(int\n10\tlen)` returns `arena_value` only if `len > 0xffff && (u16)len == 0` -- still with the literal in the asset and `.rodata`.\n11\tD17 (Name Collapse, R8-style identifier collapse) left the native track: 6-entry fixture, new per-char permutation codec\n12\t`indexed`, one renamed class `a`; the TT dex carried the real hint `follow b -> a and ignore field c` + `decoy` strings.\n13\tD18 (Encrypted Strings, `string_decryption` \"runtime string decryption\"): 6-entry fixture, codec `xor` again (b64 + 1-byte\n14\tkey); single dex had no cipher code, the TT/Mastery dex added class `EncryptedStrings` method `decryptByte` + `STRUCTURAL`.\n15\tD19 (Reflection Maze, `reflective_dispatch` \"reflective secret dispatch\"; prompt \"Reconstruct reflective dispatch across\n16\tgenerated equivalent call graphs\"): 6-entry fixture, NEW codec name `reflection` whose `data` is the plaintext answer;\n17\tclass `ReflectionMaze`, but NO reflection API in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `dispatch` + `STRUCTURAL` strings.\n18\tD20 (Loaded La