rings -a` | med |\n135\t| 87 | Attestation token (Play Integrity / SafetyNet JWS) in assets/code | gap | JWS claims (nonce, apkCertificateDigestSha256, package) or the verdict branch | `eyJ` 3-part token, `IntegrityManager`, `attest`, `ctsProfileMatch`, `deviceIntegrity` | py b64url decode; compare claims to APK cert digest | med |\n136\t\n137\t## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n138\t\n139\t```\n140\t0. Always first: python3 -c \"from lib.android import extract_answer as e;print(e('x.apk'))\"   # puzzle->zip->dex->apktool/jadx\n141\t   If it prints ANS-... and the prompt is the usual \"backend answer code\": submit. Do NOT chase 127.0.0.1:19090.\n142\t1. unzip -l x.apk   -> map the entries:\n143\t   assets/huntress_puzzle.json      puzzle codec; data already ANS-? done (D15 native, D19 reflection); new name -> data[:4] vs \"ANS-\"\n144\t                                    data = an entry path (D20 `dynamic`: assets/payload.dex)? open THAT entry, recurse from 1.\n145\t                                    int list beside data (D17 `indexed`, D5 `split`): r[order[i]] = data[i]; else gather\n146\t   lib/<abi>/*.so                   strings -a | grep ANS- ; nm -D --defined-only ; no Java_* -> JNI_OnLoad/RegisterNatives\n147\t                                    Java_*_native*(int) + *_accepts helper (D16 gate): objdump -d it; the value it returns\n148\t                                    is the answer (D16: &arena_value = the .rodata ANS- literal; bypass len 65536)\n149\t   lib/*/libapp.so + libflutter.so  Flutter: strings libapp.so; flutter_assets/kernel_blob.bin (debug = source text)\n150\t   assets/index.android.bundle      RN: head -c8 | xxd; c61fbc03 = Hermes -> hbc-decompiler; else webcrack/js-beautify\n151\t   assemblies/*.dll|*.blob, libmonodroid.so   Xamarin: XALZ = lz4 per-dll; then ilspycmd f.dll\n152\t   libil2cpp.so + global-metadata.dat         Unity IL2CPP: strings global-metadata.dat | grep ANS- ; Managed/*.dll -> ilspycmd\n153\t   assets/www/, cordova.js, capacitor.config  hybrid JS: grep -r in assets/www\n154\t   assets/*.dex|*.jar|*.apk|*.zip|*.bin       dynamic code loading (D20: plain dex, ANS- const in `...payload.Module`):\n155\t                                    strings -a it first; no dex/PK/ELF magic -> xor/known-plaintext unwrap (key from host dex);\n156\t                                    >1 payload -> the one matching the host's pinned digest; >1 ANS- -> the member the host\n157\t                                    names (`<entry>:<class>` string, `moduleContract`), never the first regex hit\n158\t   libjiagu/libsecexe/libDexHelper.so          packer: payload is the encrypted asset; static decrypt or give up early\n159\t   res/xml/network_security_config.xml        NSC: aapt dump xmltree x.apk res/xml/network_security_config.xml\n160\t   resources.arsc                   aapt dump --values resources x.apk | grep -iE 'ans-|secret|key|flag|token'\n161\t   *.db / shared_prefs/*.xml / *.ab sqlite3 f.db .dump ; .ab: dd bs=24 skip=1 | zlib-flate -uncompress | tar x\n162\t   res/raw/*.bks|*.p12|*.pem        keystore: password is a dex string; keytool -list -v -storepass PW\n163\t   google-services.json / firebase  key/URL itself may be the answer\n164\t   base.apk + split_config.*.apk / manifest.json / toc.pb / BundleConfig.pb   split/XAPK/APKS/AAB: unzip inner, recurse\n165\t   Payload/*.app/                   iOS: plistlib Info.plist; rz-bin -zz the Mach-O\n166\t2. Plain-anywhere scan (incl. UTF-16 the zip scan misses):\n167\t   for f in $(unzip -Z1 x.apk); do unzip -p x.apk \"$f\" | strings -a -el | grep -H --label=\"$f\" ANS-; done\n168\t   7z l x.apk vs unzip -l x.apk differ -> zip tricks (dup entry / trailing data): binwalk x.apk\n169\t3. Manifest (fast): aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml | grep -E \\\n170\t   'exported|scheme|host|autoVerify|permission|debuggable|allowBackup|usesCleartext|networkSecurity|taskAffinity|launchMode|meta-data'\n171\t   meta-data value= is a hiding spot (huntress.mechanic lives there). droidasc getmanifest x.apk prints the XML.\n172\t4. Dex triage: strings -a classes*.dex | grep -E 'DAY-|CODEC|ANS-|^[0-9A-F]{8,16}$' then map API hits to themes:\n173\t   DexClassLoader/InMemoryDexClassLoader/moduleContract -> asset dex   SecretKeySpec/AES/Cipher -> static key decrypt\n174\t   loadLibrary/RegisterNatives -> .so                     java/util/Random/setSeed/currentTimeMillis -> regenerate RNG\n175\t   MessageDigest/PBKDF2 -> hash brute                     addJavascriptInterface/loadUrl/file:///android_asset -> assets html/js\n176\t   Binder/$Stub/Messenger/onReceive -> IPC handler        CertificatePinner/sha256/ -> pins in code or NSC\n177\t   su/magisk/RootBeer/goldfish/frida/TracerPid -> flag sits in the gated branch: read it, never run it\n178\t   Class.forName/getDeclaredMethod -> reflection_scan     BuildConfig / R$string -> arsc / BuildConfig.java\n179\t   Proxy/InvocationHandler/MethodHandles/invoke-custom -> resolve the real target; packed-switch in a loop -> flattened CFG\n180\t   KeyStore.getInstance(\"BKS\"|\"PKCS12\") -> res/raw keystore + password string\n181\t5. Read code only after 1-4: droidasc findrefs x.apk string <hit>; droidasc getclass x.apk <cls>; jadx -d w/jadx x.apk\n182\t   (add --deobf for 1-2 letter class names). Strings split across constants: rebuild order from the method body.\n183\t   String decryptors (D18 TT `EncryptedStrings.decryptByte`): dex_eval_scan, else jadx the helper, take the ARGS from\n184\t   each call site, re-implement in py; unknown key/rolling scheme -> solve it from the ANS- known plaintext.\n185\t   R8/decoys (D17): hint strings like \"follow b -> a and ignore field c\" name the chain; >1 ANS- candidate -> keep\n186\t   the one appended before `proof=` in ChallengeActivity, never the first regex hit. Reflection/dispatch (D19 theme):\n187\t   names may be encoded or picked by a key from the deep link/asset; evaluate only the invoked target, not its twins.\n188\t   lib scanners for code-side answers (not in extract_answer): renamed_chain_scan, proof_flow_scan, dex_eval_scan,\n189\t   reflection_scan, mapping_restore_scan, signing_block_scan, zip_structure_scan  (all lib.android, take apk path)\n190\t6. Native, if no literal: rizin -A -qc 'iE; izz~ANS; afl' f.so ; pdf @ sym.Java_... ; xor loops -> py capstone/unicorn.\n191\t7. Validate: candidate must fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ (uppercase). Two sources (asset + .so) agreeing = submit.\n192\t8. Mastery: each set can be a different day's fixture; decode every APK on its own; loop over all answer_ids (3 or 5).\n193\t```\n194\t\n195\t## Readiness gaps\n196\t\n197\tPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n198\t`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built (prebuild-state ok, dropped from the list):\n199\tutf16-string-pool-scan, nested-container-recurse, dex-native-split-assembly, static-key-cipher-decode,\n200\tdecode-any-chain-peel, native-so-emulate-export, dex-string-decrypt-arrays, asset-db-prefs-backup,\n201\tidentity-derived-key, hermes-hbc-string-table, cert-and-signing-facts, il2cpp-metadata-literals,\n202\tjni-export-return-trace, jni-gate-bypass-input, registernatives-table, native-stack-string, multi-abi-arm-native,\n203\tdex-native-call-args, native-gated-branch-read, dex-gated-branch-consts, webview-asset-js-scan,\n204\tcert-pin-and-nsc-facts, puzzle-indexed-and-perm-fields, proof-flow-candidate-ranking, r8-renamed-chain-follow,\n205\tdalvik-mini-interpreter, permutation-transposition-family, reflection-name-resolve, proguard-mapping-restore,\n206\tapk-signing-block-payload, zip-structure-anomaly-scan, integrity-derived-key, ans-prefix-numeric-compose,\n207\tcustom-alphabet-decode, asset-cipher-dex-loader, native-init-array-decrypt, resource-id-const-resolve,\n208\tmessagedigest-derived-answer, v1-manifest-digest-verify, dex-slack-and-header-anomaly, aab-proto-manifest-parse,\n209\trolling-xor-keystream-family, decrypt-call-site-args-eval, known-string-obfuscator-signatures,\n210\tidentifier-collision-resolve, opaque-predicate-dead-branch, java-serialized-object-parse, jwt-token-decode-verify,\n211\tprotobuf-asset-wire-decode, sqlcipher-asset-decrypt, dispatch-key-resolve, entry-reachable-callgraph-rank,\n212\tflattened-cfg-switch-eval, proxy-methodhandle-invokecustom, clean-device-env-stubs, tiny-bytecode-vm-interpret,\n213\tjni-reflection-callback, kotlin-metadata-names-and-coroutines, dex-bytecode-integrity-gate.\n214\t\n215\t```json\n216\t[\n217\t  {\"id\": \"puzzle-entry-pointer-follow\", \"concept\": \"puzzle `data` names a zip entry (D20 codec `dynamic`, row 42)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20's generic answer() returned nothing because puzzle_candidates yields `data` verbatim (`assets/payload.dex`); only the raw_entry_scan fallback saved it. Make it first-class in lib.android: when any puzzle field (data/path/module/entry/payload/file, or any string value) equals or ends with an existing zip entry name (also with `assets/` prefix added/stripped, `file:///android_asset/` stripped), read that entry and run the full candidate chain on its bytes (dex string pool incl. multi-dex, nested zip/jar/apk via nested-container-recurse, ELF strings, magic unwrap), depth <= 3, cycle-safe. Return those candidates FIRST, and never return the pointer string itself as a candidate. Also accept host-dex strings shaped `<entry>:<dotted.Class>` as pointers.\"},\n218\t  {\"id\": \"module-contract-member-eval\", \"concept\": \"secondary-dex 'module contract': value of the host-named class/field/method in the payload (D20 TT `moduleContract`)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20 TT host dex added `moduleContract` and `assets/payload.dex:com.huntress.arena.payload.Module`; the payload had strings `ANSWER`/`CONTRACT`. When a payload holds >1 ANS- candidate the target member decides. Pure python over the payload dex (androguard or own parser): map static final fields to values (class_def static_values encoded_array + sput in <clinit>), map each method returning String to its const-string/StringBuilder result via dex_eval_scan; resolve the target from host strings (`<entry>:<Class>`, method names near `loadClass`/`getMethod`/`moduleContract`, interface method names implemented by the payload class, fields named ANSWER/CONTRACT/answer). Rank: host-named member > field named ANSWER/CONTRACT > interface impl reachable from host > others (demoted).\"},\n219\t  {\"id\": \"payload-digest-pinned-select\", \"concept\": \"'challenge-signed' secondary module: several payloads, the pinned digest/signature picks the loaded one (row 83)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20 prompt said 'challenge-signed' but shipped no verify code; the obvious next twist is N payloads (payload_a.dex, payload_b.dex, *.bin) or a decoy module. Compute for every non-META entry: SHA-256/SHA-1/MD5/CRC32 (hex upper/lower + base64 + base64url), dex header adler32/sha1 fields, the v1 MANIFEST.MF/.SF per-entry digests; collect host-dex constants (64/40/32-hex, 44-char base64, ints) and sidecar entries (`*.sig`, `*.sha256`, `*.digest`, JSON fields `sha256`/`digest`/`signature`). Select the payload whose digest matches a host/sidecar pin (also check MANIFEST.MF digest validity to reject a tampered decoy), run the candidate chain on it first, demote the rest. If a PKCS#1/Ed25519 signature + public key are shipped, verify with pycryptodome.\"},\n220\t  {\"id\": \"payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap\", \"concept\": \"encrypted/wrapped secondary payload: recover the wrapper from the expected file magic\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Next step after D20's plain payload: the asset dex/jar/so XOR'd, added, reversed, base64/hex-text, gzip/zlib/lzma, or AES with a host-dex key. Generic unwrapper: for each asset without a known magic, try known-plaintext headers (`dex\\\\n035\\\\0`..`dex\\\\n041\\\\0`, `cdex001\\\\0`, `PK\\\\x03\\\\x04`, `\\\\x7fELF\\\\x02\\\\x01\\\\x01`, `SQLite format 3\\\\0`) to derive single-byte, repeating (1-16 B, period found by consistency), add/sub and rolling (`k+i`, `k^i`) keys; verify by a full dex header check (file_size field == len, adler32 valid) or a zip central directory; also try text layers (base64/hex/reversed) and compressors first. asset-cipher-dex-loader covers AES with an explicit key -- reuse it, then recurse the decoded bytes through puzzle-entry-pointer-follow.\"},\n221\t  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n222\t  {\"id\": \"multi-stage-loader-recurse\", \"concept\": \"stage-1 payload loads/decrypts stage-2 (row 85)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Loaded later' can chain: stage-1 dex (from assets) references another entry name + key (const-string, fill-array-data) and decrypts it into stage-2 (dex, jar, zip with classes.dex, .so via System.load). After unwrapping stage 1, scan ITS strings for entry names present in the outer APK or in nested containers and for key material, feed them to payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap / static-key-cipher-decode, recurse to depth 4 with a byte budget. Report the stage path with each candidate.\"},\n223\t  {\"id\": \"classloader-shadow-resolve\", \"concept\": \"same class descriptor in host and payload dex; delegation order decides (row 84)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Index classes across classes*.dex and every payload dex; when a descriptor appears in more than one, decide which definition runs: DexClassLoader/PathClassLoader/InMemoryDexClassLoader are parent-first (host/boot copy wins) unless the app defines a ClassLoader subclass overriding loadClass/findClass (child-first) or loads via a fresh loader with a null/boot parent (const/4 null passed as parent). Evaluate only the winning definition's members; demote ANS- candidates from shadowed copies.\"},\n224\t  {\"id\": \"cdex-vdex-string-pool\", \"concept\": \"compact/optimised dex payloads (cdex001, vdex, oat) (row 86)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If a payload is CompactDex (`cdex001`) or wrapped in vdex (`vdex0xx`, holds dex/cdex sections) or an OAT ELF (`oatdata` symbol), androguard and dex_strings fail. Pure python: parse vdex section headers to extract embedded dex/cdex; for cdex, read header string_ids (offsets are relative to data_off) and decode MUTF-8 strings; for oat, locate embedded dex via `oatdata` + OatDexFile entries or by scanning for `dex\\\\n0`/`cdex` magic. Feed strings to the ANS regex and to module-contract-member-eval where possible.\"},\n225\t  {\"id\": \"native-payload-system-load\", \"concept\": \"native code loaded later: `System.load(<extracted asset .so>)` instead of lib/<abi>/\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Native twin of D20: an ELF stored under assets/ (or inside the payload dex's raw resources), possibly xor/zlib-wrapped, extracted to filesDir and loaded with System.load. Detect ELF magic in any entry (after payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap) and run the existing native chain on it (strings/.rodata, jni-export-return-trace, registernatives-table, native-so-emulate-export, native-init-array-decrypt) as if it were lib/x86_64/*.so; also handle an arm64-only payload via multi-abi-arm-native.\"},\n226\t  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n227\t  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python apkid` (needs yara-python, already OK). `apkid -j x.apk` names packers, obfuscators and anti-debug in one call: a fast routing cue for an unseen theme.\"},\n228\t  {\"id\": \"bundletool\", \"concept\": \"AAB / APKS packaging (row 58)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release jar google/bundletool (bundletool-all-1.17.x.jar) into tools/bundletool + bin shim. `bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`, `bundletool build-apks --mode=universal`. AAB manifests are protobuf, so aapt dump xmltree fails on them.\"},\n229\t  {\"id\": \"ios-ipa-readiness\", \"concept\": \"iOS IPA (row 64)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Lane is named mobile-android; if an .ipa ever ships: unzip Payload/, plistlib for Info.plist and binary plists, rz-bin -zz / lief for Mach-O strings, ipsw (github blacktop/ipsw release) for class-dump. Nothing to prebuild now.\"},\n230\t  {\"id\": \"attestation-jws-claims\", \"concept\": \"Play Integrity / SafetyNet attestation token shipped in the app (row 87)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"MASVS-RESILIENCE leftover after loader/integrity days. Find 3-part `eyJ...` JWS strings in dex/assets/JSON; b64url-decode header + payload; report claims (nonce, apkPackageName, apkCertificateDigestSha256, ctsProfileMatch/basicIntegrity, requestDetails/appIntegrity/deviceIntegrity verdicts, tokenPayloadExternal). Compare the cert digest claim with the APK's signing cert (cert-and-signing-facts) and the package name; if the answer is derived (HMAC of nonce, verdict-gated branch), hand the claim values to dex-gated-branch-consts / messagedigest-derived-answer. Verify x5c chain/signature with pycryptodome when a cert is embedded.\"},\n231\t  {\"id\": \"xamarin-xalz-blob-unpack\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ lz4 (row 55)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Pure python so no pyxamstore is needed in-window: XALZ per-assembly (magic `XALZ`, u32 descriptor index, u32 uncompressed size, lz4.block payload), assemblies.blob `XABA` (header, assembly descriptors with data offset/size, optional hash tables) and .NET 8 `libassemblies.<abi>.blob.so` (payload in an ELF section `payload`). Output each DLL; scan its #US user-string heap (UTF-16) for ANS- via the existing utf16 pool scan.\"},\n232\t  {\"id\": \"il2cppdumper\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release Perfare/Il2CppDumper (or SamboyCoding/Cpp2IL) into tools/; run with bin/dotnet. Only if a Unity fixture ever ships.\"},\n233\t  {\"id\": \"blutter\", \"concept\": \"Flutter Dart AOT (row 52)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github worawit/blutter (python3 blutter.py <lib dir> <out>; builds per Dart version with cmake/ninja + fetches the Dart SDK, slow first run; arm64 only). Alt: pip reflutter (needs repack + device: low value). Plain strings on libapp.so cover literal answers.\"},\n234\t  {\"id\": \"abe\", \"concept\": \"encrypted Android backup (row 16)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release nelenkov/android-backup-extractor (abe.jar): `java -jar abe.jar unpack b.ab b.tar [pw]`. Needed only for encrypted .ab (PBKDF2+AES); unencrypted is zlib-flate.\"},\n235\t  {\"id\": \"frida-tools\", \"concept\": \"dynamic instrumentation / root and frida checks (rows 47, 48)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip frida-tools / objection. Low value: no Android device or emulator here (adb present, no target), and every answer so far was static. Keep the rule: read the gated branch statically.\"},\n236\t  {\"id\": \"standalone-baksmali\", \"concept\": \"smali-level reading / patching (row 51)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"Link tools/dex2jar/d2j-baksmali.sh + d2j-smali.sh into bin/ (already on disk), or github google/smali release. apktool d already emits smali, so cosmetic.\"}\n237\t]\n238\t```\n239\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5590372-5ad7-47d3-aa84-1c0838c43c34","uuid":"33c3bd94-9baa-4bca-a7dc-adcd8dc6deda","timestamp":"2026-10-21T13:18:32.608Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/mobile-android.md","content":"# mobile-android: coverage atlas (D1-D20 seen, D21+ forecast)\n\nScope: common Android/mobile CTF concepts mapped against what this lane has shipped and what the harness can handle.\nGround truth (see `reference/techniques/mobile-android.md`): all 20 days shipped the same ~12.7 KB fixture. The day's\nTHEME was flavour only (manifest `huntress.mechanic` + dex `DAY-NN:<theme>:<mechanic>`). The answer `ANS-<16 HEX>` was\nin `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` behind a rotating codec (plain/reverse/base64/xor/split/hex/caesar/native/indexed/\nreflection) on D1-D19. D15\nadded the first real extra payload (`lib/x86_64/libarena.so` with the answer as a `.rodata` literal) and mixed-day\nMastery. D16 (JNI Boundary) TT/Mastery builds added the first REAL gate in code: `Java_<pkg>_JNIBoundary_nativeEvidence(int\nlen)` returns `arena_value` only if `len > 0xffff && (u16)len == 0` -- still with the literal in the asset and `.rodata`.\nD17 (Name Collapse, R8-style identifier collapse) left the native track: 6-entry fixture, new per-char permutation codec\n`indexed`, one renamed class `a`; the TT dex carried the real hint `follow b -> a and ignore field c` + `decoy` strings.\nD18 (Encrypted Strings, `string_decryption` \"runtime string decryption\"): 6-entry fixture, codec `xor` again (b64 + 1-byte\nkey); single dex had no cipher code, the TT/Mastery dex added class `EncryptedStrings` method `decryptByte` + `STRUCTURAL`.\nD19 (Reflection Maze, `reflective_dispatch` \"reflective secret dispatch\"; prompt \"Reconstruct reflective dispatch across\ngenerated equivalent call graphs\"): 6-entry fixture, NEW codec name `reflection` whose `data` is the plaintext answer;\nclass `ReflectionMaze`, but NO reflection API in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `dispatch` + `STRUCTURAL` strings.\nD20 (Loaded Later, `dynamic_dex` \"secondary DEX loading\"; prompt \"Analyze a challenge-signed secondary DEX and recover\nthe module contract\"): 7-entry APK with `assets/payload.dex` (508 B, plain dex 035); NEW codec `dynamic` whose `data` is\nthe ENTRY PATH `assets/payload.dex` -- the FIRST day the answer left the JSON value: a plain `ANS-` const in payload class\n`com.huntress.arena.payload.Module` (strings `ANSWER`, `CONTRACT`, `DAY20-SIGNED-MODULE:..`). No ClassLoader/verify code\nin any host dex; TT/Mastery host dex added `moduleContract` + `assets/payload.dex:com.huntress.arena.payload.Module`.\nSo \"seen Dn\" below means the THEME was named that day. It does NOT mean an exploit was ever needed.\nThe risk for D21+ is the **answer moving further from the JSON** (D20: one hop, still a literal) more than the theme.\nD15-D20 read as a MASVS-RESILIENCE / obfuscation arc (native secret -> JNI gate -> name obfuscation + decoys -> string\nencryption -> reflection -> dynamic code loading). Next expect: the payload ENCRYPTED/wrapped (key in host dex, unwrap by\nmagic known plaintext), \"challenge-signed\" made real (several payloads, only the one whose digest/signature matches a\npinned value is loaded), >1 `ANS-` in the payload with the host-named member (`moduleContract`) deciding, class shadowing\nbetween host and payload loaders, multi-stage loaders, anti-tamper / root / emulator / debugger / Frida checks, and\ncontrol-flow flattening or a tiny VM. New codecs keep arriving (d7 caesar, d15 native, d17 indexed, d19 reflection, d20\ndynamic) and old ones recur (d18 xor): check `data` for `ANS-`, then for an entry name, then decode from `ANS-` alone.\n\nTool status (after `source bin/env.sh`; checked 2026-10-15). INSTALLED: jadx 1.5.6, apktool 3.0.3, aapt, aapt2,\napksigner, keytool, jarsigner, d2j-dex2jar (+ `tools/dex2jar/d2j-*.sh`: baksmali, decrypt-string, ...), droidasc,\nandroguard (CLI + py), apkInspector, rizin/rz-bin, r2/rabin2, Ghidra `analyzeHeadless`, readelf/nm/strings, hbc-decompiler/\nhbc-disassembler/hbc-file-parser (hermes-dec), ilspycmd + dotnet, webcrack, js-beautify, sqlite3, 7z, binwalk, yara,\ntshark, zlib-flate, openssl, adb (no device). py: lief, pyelftools, capstone, unicorn, pycryptodome, lz4, plistlib.\nMISSING: blutter, reFlutter, pyxamstore, Il2CppDumper/Cpp2IL, frida/frida-tools/objection, apkid, apkleaks, bundletool,\nabe (android-backup-extractor), standalone baksmali/smali, dexdump, zipalign, de4dot, ipsw/plistutil/class-dump.\nTimed constraint: `solve.py` may use only stdlib + lib.* + pyzipper/pyelftools/pefile/capstone/pycryptodome/androguard,\nno subprocess, <1 s per set. Prebuilt extractors must be pure python.\n\n## Concept table\n\nLegend: tool `[i]` = installed here, `[M]` = missing. \"puzzle\" = `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` (`lib.android.puzzle_candidates`).\n\n| # | concept | status | where the answer likely hides | recognition cues | standard tool + exact command | D21+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Exported Activity / implicit-export default | seen D1 | puzzle; real CTFs: `onCreate` reveals the flag when started with a magic extra | `android:exported=\"true\"`, intent-filter w/o `exported` + targetSdk<31 | `aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml` [i]; `droidasc getmanifest x.apk` [i]; `lib.android.manifest_facts` | high: Mastery mixes old days |\n| 2 | Exported Service / AIDL / Messenger | gap | `onBind`/`onStartCommand`/`handleMessage` compares + returns secret | `<service exported>`, `extends Binder`, `$Stub`, `IInterface`, `Messenger` | `jadx -d out x.apk` [i]; `droidasc findrefs x.apk type Landroid/os/Binder;` | med: next IPC theme |\n| 3 | Broadcast receiver (exported, dynamic, ordered/sticky) | gap | `onReceive` action/extra check; action strings in dex | `<receiver exported>`, `registerReceiver`, `sendOrderedBroadcast`, custom `ACTION_*` | `aapt dump xmltree ...`; `jadx` grep `onReceive` | med-high: classic unused IPC theme |\n| 4 | Content provider (SQLi, path traversal, FileProvider paths) | seen D6 | puzzle; real: `query()` / `openFile()`, `res/xml/*paths*.xml` | `<provider exported grantUriPermissions>`, `UriMatcher`, `<root-path>`, `../` | `apktool d -f -o out x.apk` [i]; `aapt dump xmltree x.apk res/xml/file_paths.xml` | med (mixed Mastery) |\n| 5 | Custom permission weakness (normal level, typo, missing) | gap | manifest | `<permission protectionLevel=\"normal\">`, `android:permission` on comp vs `uses-permission` | `aapt dump permissions x.apk` [i] | med |\n| 6 | Task hijacking / StrandHogg | gap | manifest attrs (answer = static) | `taskAffinity`, `allowTaskReparenting=\"true\"`, `launchMode=\"singleTask\"` | `aapt dump xmltree ... \\| grep -E 'taskAffinity\\|launchMode\\|Reparent'` | med |\n| 7 | Tapjacking / overlay | gap | layout XML or manifest | `filterTouchesWhenObscured`, `FLAG_WINDOW_IS_OBSCURED`, `SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW` | `apktool d` then `grep -r filterTouches out/res` | med |\n| 8 | Deep link (custom scheme, param parsing) | seen D2 | puzzle; real: `getQueryParameter` branch | `<data android:scheme=..>`, `getData()`, `getQueryParameter` | `droidasc findrefs x.apk string <scheme>` [i]; `jadx` | high (mixed) |\n| 9 | App Links / autoVerify / assetlinks | gap | host + cert SHA-256 (assetlinks needs the signing fp) | `android:autoVerify=\"true\"`, `https` scheme+host | `apksigner verify --print-certs x.apk` [i]; `keytool -printcert -jarfile x.apk` [i] | med |\n| 10 | Intent redirection / nested Intent / `Intent.parseUri` | seen D3 | puzzle; real: forwarded Intent reaches a private comp | `getParcelableExtra(..Intent)`, `startActivity(`, `parseUri`, `intent://` | `jadx`; `droidasc findrefs x.apk method parseUri` | high (mixed) |\n| 11 | PendingIntent (mutable / implicit base) | seen D4 | puzzle | `FLAG_MUTABLE`, `PendingIntent.getActivity` with empty Intent | `strings -a classes.dex \\| grep -i pendingintent` | high (mixed) |\n| 12 | Fragment injection (PreferenceActivity) | gap | `isValidFragment` returns true | `PreferenceActivity`, `:android:show_fragment` | `jadx` | low |\n| 13 | WebView JS interface | seen D7 | puzzle; real: `@JavascriptInterface` getter returns secret | `addJavascriptInterface`, `@JavascriptInterface` | `jadx`; `droidasc findrefs x.apk method addJavascriptInterface` | high (mixed) |\n| 14 | WebView file access / UXSS / loadUrl from extra | gap | `assets/*.html`/`*.js` holding the secret, or the URL itself | `setAllowUniversalAccessFromFileURLs(true)`, `file:///android_asset/`, `loadUrl(getIntent()` | `unzip -l x.apk 'assets/*'`; `unzip -p x.apk 'assets/*.html'` | med-high |\n| 15 | WebView URL-allowlist bypass (`shouldOverrideUrlLoading`) | gap | allowlist check strings | `startsWith(\"https://`, `endsWith(`, `getHost()`, `loadDataWithBaseURL` | `jadx` | med |\n| 16 | allowBackup / adb backup `.ab` | seen D5 | puzzle; real: `*.ab` -> tar -> `sp/*.xml`/`db/*.db` | `allowBackup=\"true\"`, `fullBackupContent`, `dataExtractionRules`, header `ANDROID BACKUP` | `dd if=b.ab bs=24 skip=1 \\| zlib-flate -uncompress \\| tar x` [i]; abe [M] | med |\n| 17 | SharedPreferences secrets | seen D11 | puzzle; real: `shared_prefs/*.xml` or dex default value | `getSharedPreferences`, `MODE_WORLD_READABLE`, `EncryptedSharedPreferences` | `unzip -l`; `jadx` | high (mixed) |\n| 18 | SQLite / Room / Realm | seen D12 | puzzle; real: `assets/*.db` row, `rawQuery` | `SQLiteOpenHelper`, `rawQuery`, magic `SQLite format 3\\0`, `.realm` | `sqlite3 f.db .dump` [i] | med |\n| 19 | External storage / world-readable files | gap | path constant + file in assets | `getExternalStorageDirectory`,