{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFTBKJ2y2pfbPvHq1meL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018i5WhLQ5wVviSMfAf9s2ze","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/mobile-android.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold_built=\"\"\"jni-reflection-callback, kotlin-metadata-names-and-coroutines, dex-bytecode-integrity-gate.\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old_built)==1\ns=s.replace(old_built,\"\"\"jni-reflection-callback, kotlin-metadata-names-and-coroutines, dex-bytecode-integrity-gate, module-contract-member-eval,\npayload-digest-pinned-select, payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap, multi-stage-loader-recurse, classloader-shadow-resolve,\ncdex-vdex-string-pool, native-payload-system-load, attestation-jws-claims, xamarin-xalz-blob-unpack.\nPending retry: puzzle-entry-pointer-follow (attempt 1 failed only on an unrelated script-lane fixture timing test).\"\"\")\na=s.index(\"```json\\n\")+len(\"```json\\n\"); b=s.index(\"```\",a)\ngaps=json.loads(s[a:b])\nbuilt={'module-contract-member-eval','payload-digest-pinned-select','payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap','multi-stage-loader-recurse','classloader-shadow-resolve','cdex-vdex-string-pool','native-payload-system-load','attestation-jws-claims','xamarin-xalz-blob-unpack'}\nkeep={g['id']:g for g in gaps if g['id'] not in built}\npf=keep.pop('puzzle-entry-pointer-follow')\npf['priority']=2\npf['detail']+=\" D21 went back to an in-JSON codec, so this is a Mastery-mix safeguard (the d20 set recurs), not the next escalation; the 2026-10-20 attempt failed only on tests/test_lane_fixtures.py timing for a script fixture -- rerun.\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path\",\"concept\":\"anti-debug STATE MACHINE whose clean terminal state emits the answer (D21 prompt; rows 41, 79, 89)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D21 named 'a clean-room anti-debug state machine ... retaining the intended app flow' and the TT dex added `debuggerGate`, but no code shipped yet. Build `anti_debug_state_scan(apk)`: find methods with a state variable (int local/field, enum ordinal, String state) reassigned inside a loop or across a packed/sparse-switch, where at least one transition depends on a probe that clean_device_scan stubs (Debug.isDebuggerConnected/waitingForDebugger, ApplicationInfo.flags & 2, TracerPid, timing deltas, Settings ADB_ENABLED). Run flattened_cfg_scan's evaluator with the clean_device probe table in the same run (one combined env), starting from the initial state set in <init>/<clinit>/onCreate, until a terminal state (loop exit / return / value appended before `proof=`). Report each terminal value with its state path; rank the clean path first and DEMOTE values reached only when a probe says 'debugged' (decoy/trap/honeypot). Budget <0.8 s, never raise.\"},\n {\"id\":\"timing-and-debug-flag-probe-stubs\",\"concept\":\"timing anti-debug + debug-flag probes not yet stubbed by clean_device_scan (rows 41, 50, 88)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"clean_device_scan (built) answers Build/su/frida/TracerPid/isDebuggerConnected/ApplicationInfo.flags, but not clocks or debug settings. Extend its probe table (or add a sibling pass reusing _ENV_*): SystemClock.elapsedRealtime/uptimeMillis/elapsedRealtimeNanos, System.nanoTime/currentTimeMillis, Debug.threadCpuTimeNanos -> a monotonic counter advancing by a small fixed step (1 ms / 1e6 ns) per call so 'delta < threshold' passes; Settings.Global/Secure.getInt(ADB_ENABLED|DEVELOPMENT_SETTINGS_ENABLED|adb_enabled, def) -> 0; SystemProperties/System.getProperty('ro.debuggable'|'ro.secure'|'service.adb.root') -> '0'/'1'/'0'; BuildConfig.DEBUG static -> read its encoded static value but ALSO report the release (false) path; Debug.isDebuggerConnected on android.os.Debug and VMDebug.isDebuggingEnabled -> false; Thread.sleep no-op. Test with a synthetic dex where the answer xor key depends on the delta check.\"},\n {\"id\":\"hook-framework-introspection-stubs\",\"concept\":\"Frida/Xposed/Substrate detection via stack traces, thread names, native-method flags (row 91)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Likely next resilience theme after anti-debug. Stub for the Dalvik evaluator: Thread.currentThread().getStackTrace()/new Throwable().getStackTrace() -> a short clean array (dalvik.system.VMStack, java.lang.Thread, the app's own frames from the call chain; no de.robv.android.xposed.XposedBridge, com.saurik.substrate); Thread.getAllStackTraces keys with names 'main','FinalizerDaemon' (no 'gum-js-loop','gmain','pool-frida'); File('/proc/self/task').listFiles + comm reads -> clean names; Modifier.isNative(Method.getModifiers()) on app methods -> false; ClassLoader.loadClass/Class.forName of hook classes -> ClassNotFoundException into the method's handler; /proc/self/fd readlink -> no 'linjector'/'frida-pipe'; System.getenv('CLASSPATH'/'LD_PRELOAD') -> null. Feed into clean_device_scan's run set; same ranking (clean path first).\"},\n {\"id\":\"enum-switchmap-state-resolve\",\"concept\":\"enum/sealed state machines compiled to `$SwitchMap$` / Kotlin `$WhenMappings` (row 89)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"javac compiles `switch(enumValue)` to a synthetic class `<Outer>$1` with static int[] `$SwitchMap$<pkg>$<Enum>` filled in <clinit> by `sget-object Enum.X; invoke-virtual ordinal(); const/4 k; aput` (each under a NoSuchFieldError catch); kotlinc emits `<Outer>$WhenMappings` with `$EnumSwitchMapping$0`. The Dalvik evaluator must (1) run the enum's <clinit> (new-instance Enum(name, ordinal) + values array), (2) run the switch-map <clinit>, (3) resolve `aget` of the map by ordinal before the packed-switch. Pure python over androguard or own dex parser; expose `switchmap_table(apk)` and make dalvik-mini-interpreter / flattened_cfg_scan / anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path use it. Also handle String-switch (hashCode sparse-switch + equals) already in dispatch-key-resolve.\"},\n {\"id\":\"native-libc-probe-stubs-emulate\",\"concept\":\"native anti-debug inside the `.so` (ptrace TRACEME, /proc/self/status TracerPid, prctl, fork watchdog) during unicorn emulation (row 66)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"If D21's theme returns natively (JNI export gated by a native anti-debug probe), native_so_emulate_export / native_gate_branch_scan must survive libc calls. Add PLT/import stubs for the unicorn runner: ptrace -> 0 (first TRACEME succeeds), getppid -> zygote pid, prctl -> 0, fork -> -1 or child-never-runs, open/fopen/openat of /proc/self/status|/proc/<pid>/status -> a fake FILE yielding 'TracerPid:\\\\t0', fgets/read/fscanf/strstr/strncmp/atoi over it, /proc/self/maps without frida/xposed lines, access/stat on su/frida paths -> -1 ENOENT, kill/raise/abort/exit -> stop emulation as 'trap path', time/clock_gettime/gettimeofday -> monotonic small step, pthread_create -> run the start routine inline once or skip. Resolve imports via pyelftools .rela.plt; x86_64 first, arm64 via multi-abi path. Report the export's return string/byte buffer on the clean path.\"},\n {\"id\":\"exception-driven-control-flow\",\"concept\":\"probe throws, catch handler selects the path (row 90)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Anti-debug/anti-tamper code often uses try/catch as control flow (throw custom SecurityException when a probe trips; handler sets state or picks a decoy). Make the Dalvik evaluator model dex try_item/encoded_catch_handler tables fully: `throw` vX transfers to the first handler whose type is a supertype (walk the in-dex class hierarchy + a small java.lang exception tree), `move-exception` binds it, catch-all handlers, nested tries, and exceptions thrown by stubbed APIs (NameNotFound, ClassNotFound, FileNotFound, NumberFormat, ArithmeticException on div-int by zero, ArrayIndexOutOfBounds, NullPointerException on a null receiver). Verify with synthetic dexes where the ANS- value is only produced in a handler and where a decoy sits in the handler of a debugged-path throw.\"},\n {\"id\":\"emulator-telephony-sensor-stubs\",\"concept\":\"emulator detection beyond Build fields: telephony, sensors, battery, qemu pipes (row 48)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Extend the clean-device probe table with retail-phone answers: TelephonyManager.getDeviceId/getImei/getSubscriberId/getLine1Number/getNetworkOperatorName/getSimOperatorName/getPhoneType/getSimState (non-zero IMEI-shaped, 'T-Mobile', PHONE_TYPE_GSM, SIM_STATE_READY), SensorManager.getSensorList(TYPE_ALL) -> 20+ entries with vendor names (not 'Goldfish'), getDefaultSensor -> non-null, BatteryManager/ACTION_BATTERY_CHANGED -> level 63, temperature 285, not always charging; File.exists on /dev/qemu_pipe, /dev/socket/qemud, /system/lib/libc_malloc_debug_qemu.so, /sys/qemu_trace, /dev/goldfish_pipe -> false; /proc/cpuinfo without 'Goldfish'/'hypervisor'; Build.HARDWARE/BOARD/BOOTLOADER/HOST/SERIAL real-device values; NetworkInterface without 10.0.2.15/eth0-only. Same scan integration as clean_device_scan.\"},\n {\"id\":\"biometric-auth-callback-eval\",\"concept\":\"MASVS-AUTH biometric / local auth bypass: the success callback holds the secret (row 92)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Untouched MASVS group. Find classes extending androidx.biometric.BiometricPrompt$AuthenticationCallback, android.hardware.biometrics.BiometricPrompt$AuthenticationCallback or FingerprintManager(Compat)$AuthenticationCallback, KeyguardManager.createConfirmDeviceCredentialIntent + onActivityResult(RESULT_OK). Evaluate onAuthenticationSucceeded(result) with a result whose getCryptoObject() returns null (event-bound bypass) AND with a CryptoObject wrapping a stub Cipher (doFinal = identity) -- report both values labelled; evaluate onActivityResult with resultCode -1. Also flag `setUserAuthenticationRequired(false)` / missing `setInvalidatedByBiometricEnrollment`. ANS- regex on the results; demote values reached only on onAuthenticationFailed/onAuthenticationError.\"},\n {\"id\":\"binder-ontransact-code-map\",\"concept\":\"bound Service / AIDL / Messenger: transaction code -> reply value (row 2)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Still-unused IPC surface. For every exported <service> (manifest_facts) find its Binder: classes extending android.os.Binder or `I*$Stub` overriding onTransact(int code, Parcel data, Parcel reply, int flags), and Handler subclasses used by Messenger (handleMessage(Message) switching on msg.what). Evaluate per case of the packed/sparse-switch on code/what (incl. FIRST_CALL_TRANSACTION = 1 offsets and the interface descriptor `enforceInterface` string) with a stub Parcel (readString/readInt return the constants the case compares against when solvable), collecting reply.writeString / Bundle.putString / Message.obtain(..., obj) values. Report code -> value; ANS- regex; prefer the code named in strings/manifest/meta-data.\"},\n {\"id\":\"broadcast-receiver-action-map\",\"concept\":\"exported / dynamic broadcast receiver: (action, extras) -> emitted value (row 3)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Find <receiver> components (exported, intent-filter actions, permission) and dynamic registerReceiver(IntentFilter(action)) calls; evaluate onReceive(Context, Intent) per declared action with a stub Intent whose getAction returns that action and getStringExtra/getIntExtra return the constant the code compares against (solve simple equals/== guards from const-strings in the same method), collecting setResultData/setResultExtras/Log/sendBroadcast extras/SharedPreferences.putString values. Handles ordered broadcasts (getResultData chaining). Output action -> value; ANS- regex.\"},\n {\"id\":\"dart-snapshot-string-pool\",\"concept\":\"Flutter release `libapp.so`: strings in the Dart AOT snapshot (row 52)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail