{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFTFi3dZVqr8KakhZ3AG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I updated both mobile-android files and touched nothing else. No tests, submits or GM calls were run.\n\n- **`reference/techniques/mobile-android.md`** (199 lines): Added the day21 entry for \"Debug Me If You Can\". The APK was the plain 6-entry fixture with the `reverse` codec, so day20's pointer to a second dex didn't continue. It was also the first APK in the lane with `android:debuggable=\"true\"`. There was no anti-debug code and no state machine in it; only the Time Trial dex added a `debuggerGate` string. The race probe got CORRECT in about 3 s, and Time Trial (2.23 s in-window) and Mastery (2.10 s) were both correct on the first try. In Variant axes I added a new \"Manifest flags\" axis and this day's codec, Mastery day mix and dex-size data. I also added a recognition-cue row for the anti-debug theme and two pitfalls: escalation isn't monotonic, and a manifest flag is not an answer.\n- **`reference/coverage/mobile-android.md`** (255 lines): Anti-debug and debuggable are now marked `seen D21` (theme only), and I added table rows 88–92: timing anti-debug, enum state machines, exception-driven control flow, Frida/Xposed detection and biometric bypass.\n- **Readiness gaps:** I moved the 9 gaps the prebuild finished last night to the built list and put 12 not-yet-built prebuild gaps in the queue, with \"Recognition cues\" at 58 lines. The new priority 1 gaps cover the anti-debug state machine, timing and debug-flag stubs, Frida/Xposed introspection, enum switch maps, and libc stubs for native emulation. `puzzle-entry-pointer-follow` dropped to priority 2 and is marked for a retry; its only failure was an unrelated timing test in another lane's fixtures."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":829,"cache_read